https://view.news.eu.nasdaq.com/view?id=be6781ef91f2f49052c6bf8157ed94a72&lang=en&src=listed
  BODY: third quarter, net sales increased by 12.4% and operating result by 2.1%. Profitability improved in the Baltic businesses in particular, while Finland’s result was weighed down by the weak demand during the summer season. </span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>Olvi’s market shares remained at a good level in tight price competition. However, the market has not strengthened in line with our expectations, and the third quarter did not bring the expected boost to consumer demand. Market conditions are expected to remain unchanged for the rest of the year. </span><span>&nbsp;</span><span>In Denmark, the business remains loss-making. The cost pressures caused by the geopolitical situation are not expected to ease, either. For these reasons, we have lowered our expectations for the 2026 result.</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>The business development in Denmark is weaker than targeted. Measures to improve profitability are on-going, but their impact on the result is materialising slower than expected. In Denmark, we are continuing our efforts to increase the production capacity utilisation, acquire new production volume and strengthen our commercial position. At the same time, we are also evaluating other structural options to improve the profitability of the business.</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span><em>Growth through acquisitions</em></span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>The previously announced acquisitions, most recently the acquisition of Värska Originaal in Estonia, have been completed and consolidated into the Group's operating result (Värska Originaal as of July, the others as of January). The new companies have already boosted volume and net sales growth, and their impact on profit is positive. The impact on profit is expected to strengthen from 2027 onwards as synergies materialise.</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>The integration of the new companies is progressing as planned and is expected to continue until the end of the current year. The integrations will result in non-recurring costs for 2026 as well as additional depreciation arising from purchase price allocations. </span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>Through acquisitions, we seek long-term profitable growth and the strengthening of shareholder value. We see growth opportunities in several product categories in new geographical markets in particular. </span></p> <p style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:10pt; margin-bottom:0pt; margin-top:0pt; text-align:justify"><span>&nbs
